<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sarno River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sarno is a short river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a>, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, flowing from springs near the town of Sarno across a fertile plain to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-naples">Bay of Naples</a> near Torre Annunziata. In antiquity <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompeii">Pompeii</a> stood near its mouth and served as the port for towns of the valley such as Nuceria. Industrial and agricultural waste has made it one of the most polluted rivers in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p></div>
